Hi!

Is possible to put an shiny application using the slidify without using rCharts. I'm trying to put a graph using the graphics packages in my presentation slidify unsuccessfully. I'll put in my resume script.

---
title       : Distribuição Normal e Normal padrão
subtitle    : Universidade Estadual de Santa Cruz
author      : Ivan Bezerra Allaman
job         : Laboratório de Estatística Computacional (LEC)
framework   : io2012        # {io2012, html5slides, shower, dzslides, ...}
highlighter : highlight.js  # {highlight.js, prettify, highlight}
hitheme     : tomorrow      #
widgets     : [shiny]            # {mathjax, quiz, bootstrap}
mode        : selfcontained # {standalone, draft}
knit        : slidify::knit2slides
---

```{r opts.label = 'shiny'}
slidifyUI(
  sidebarPanel(
    sliderInput('n',
                'Tamanho da população',
               min = 2,
               max = 500,
               value = 3),

    checkboxInput("showcurve", "Mostrar curva", FALSE)
  ),
  mainPanel(
#tags$div(id = 'hist',class='shiny-html-output nvd3 rChart')
tags$div(id = 'hist', class='shiny-plot-output')
  )
)
```

app1.R

require(fdth)

output$hist <- renderPlot({
  tab = fdt(rnorm(input$n,
                  1.75,
                  0.1))
  n1 <- plot(tab,
             ylab = 'Frequência absoluta',
             xlab = 'Intervalo de classes')
  n1$set(dom = 'hist', width = 600)
  n1
})

Thank's!

