MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I need to be able to determine which shiny object has most recently changed, on the server side. For instance, I have a data table displaying some search results linked to two different text inputs. For aesthetic reasons, I would like to avoid having a data table for each input. Instead I would like to detect which text input has most recently changed and update the table accordingly.

For example:

output$my.table <- renderDataTable({
   input$a
   input$b
   if( mostRecent(input$a) ) {
      ... do something
   } else {
      ... do something else
  }
})

Any idea how to solve this that doesn't use a global, shared variable that tracks which one fired most recently?

